{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicCharacterNonvanishing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicCharacterNonvanishing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.protonResidueRealization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.protonResidueRealization","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L123-L139","doc":"**A concrete realization, so nothing above is vacuous.**\n\n`χ(A) = 8` is the QOU proton collapse constant `a₀(-1) + 2·a₁(-1)` as\n*measured* from `habiro-coefficients-atomic.witness.json` (`a₀ = 8`\nidentically, `a₁(-1) = 0`) — the value bean `qou-lrnd` corrected the\ncorpus's `4` to on 2026-08-23.  Under it the vanishing locus is `p = 2`\nalone, so the character is non-trivial at every odd prime.\n\nDeliberately a `def`, **not** an `instance`.  As an instance it would be\nfound by typeclass resolution for every downstream\n`[MotivicResidueRealization]` hypothesis, silently discharging the very\nassumption this file exists to keep visible.  It witnesses inhabitation\nand derives no physics. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.ne_zero_of_isUnit_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.ne_zero_of_isUnit_residue","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L111-L121","doc":"**Non-unitness and non-vanishing are not the same claim** — over `ZMod p`\na unit is nonzero, so `IsUnit` *delivers* the block's conclusion while\nrefuting the corpus's non-unit framing of it.\n\nApplied to `HabiroCollapse.isUnit_four_zmod`, this is the reconciliation:\nthe residue's being a unit at every odd prime is exactly why the\nnon-unit route dies (bean `qou-lrnd`) and exactly why the non-vanishing\nroute lives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.residue_ne_zero_of_gt_abs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.residue_ne_zero_of_gt_abs","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L96-L109","doc":"**The obstruction is perpetual: every prime above `|χ(A)|` is a\nnon-vanishing place.**\n\nThis is the \"almost every finite place\" shape the block claims, made\nquantitative.  A prime at which the residue vanishes must divide the\nnonzero integer `χ(A)`, hence is bounded by `|χ(A)|`; so the exceptional\nset is contained in the finitely many primes up to that bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.residue_ne_zero_of_not_dvd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.residue_ne_zero_of_not_dvd","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L90-L94","doc":"**The sketch's final step, derived.**  `p ∤ χ(A)` forces the local trace\nto be non-zero mod `p`, hence the character at `p` is non-trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.residue_eq_zero_iff_dvd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.residue_eq_zero_iff_dvd","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L80-L88","doc":"**The residue vanishes exactly at the primes dividing `χ(A)`.**\n\nStated as an `iff` on purpose: it fixes the vanishing locus completely\nrather than bounding it on one side, so no later reader can mistake the\nnon-vanishing result below for a one-directional estimate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicResidueRealization.residue_eq_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicResidueRealization.residue_eq_chi","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L76-L76","doc":"INPUT — the sketch's own step: *\"a Frobenius character whose trace\nequals `χ(A) mod p`\"*.  This is the substantive content and is a\nhypothesis, not a theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicResidueRealization.residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicResidueRealization.residue","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The trace of the local Frobenius character `χ^mot_{A,p}` after\nrealization `ρ_p`, living in the residue ring at `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicResidueRealization.chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicResidueRealization.chi","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The Euler characteristic `χ(A)`, i.e. `tr(κ₀)` via `thm:qu-to-qou`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicResidueRealization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicResidueRealization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicResidueRealization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicResidueRealization","kind":"class","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L63-L76","doc":"**§3b-cond context for the sketch's mod-`p` step.**\n\nFields are the *inputs* of the sketch, never its conclusion.  There is\ndeliberately no non-vanishing field: that is derived below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.nontrivialZModPrime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.nontrivialZModPrime","kind":"instance","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L58-L61","doc":"A prime residue ring has at least two elements, so `IsUnit` implies `≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.neZeroCoePrime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.neZeroCoePrime","kind":"instance","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicCharacterNonvanishing.lean#L55-L56","doc":"A prime is nonzero as a natural, so `ZMod p` is a genuine residue ring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}